## Reasons (checked)
R-a  Writer: the compiler writes version 1 with body_base64/body_length/body_sha256; no value, redacted, value_sha256.
R-b  Replay: body/1 needs the body keys; a version 2 record gives {:error, :body_digest_mismatch} (confirmed by a diagnostic case, see below).
R-c  --stored: the DL-102 check reads body_base64; a version 2 record counts as a failing value of every literal/constructor field, so the build blocks.
R-d  --stored: stored_version does not read the key version; a version 1 record builds (P6).

